;; The capability grant the Kotoba compiler (amu) holds when it runs as a
;; program -- the abilities its own modules name (superproject
;; adr-2609242330 S5). scripts/measure-selfhost-distance.cljk passes this as
;; `--policy` on the project route, so a compiler module that names an
;; ability is admitted with the authority the compiler actually has, and a
;; refusal on the scoreboard is a language wall rather than "no grant was
;; given to a measurement".
;;
;; Every entry is a catalog capability (lang/capability-catalog.edn) with a
;; handler in the nbb mechanism layer (amu src/kotoba/compiler/nbb/host/).
;; All but hash/sha256 also have a Linux static ELF handler (adr-2609251400
;; C3). hash/sha256 is answered by the kexe loader (wire 3) and has no C3
;; handler yet; the pure org-nist-sha2 computes the same value, and amu
;; test/nbb/host_abilities.cljk pins that the nbb handler agrees with it.
;; process/spawn and entropy/draw join when a compiler module names them.
;;
;; Eight entries, not nine: fs/browse (wire 34) is left out although both
;; runtimes answer it, because no compiler module names it yet and a policy
;; with nine or more grants is refused by amu (measured 2026-09-25 at amu
;; 8260750a: nine grants answer `internal compiler error` from `check`,
;; eight are admitted -- the same limit adr-2609251400 C1 records as
;; "malformed" on the compile route). Add it when a module needs it and the
;; limit is understood.
{:allow #{[:cap/call :cli/args]
          [:cap/call :clock/now]
          [:cap/call :env/read]
          [:cap/call :fs/app-data]
          [:cap/call :hash/sha256]
          [:cap/call :io/read]
          [:cap/call :io/write]
          [:cap/call :io/write-error]}}
